WordPress writes no log on this site: WP_DEBUG_LOG is off, the normal case on a live site. Vigie writes nothing on the server.
To turn it on yourself, in wp-config.php, before the line "That's all, stop editing":
  define( 'WP_DEBUG', true );
  define( 'WP_DEBUG_LOG', true );
  define( 'WP_DEBUG_DISPLAY', false );
WordPress advises against it on a live site: give WP_DEBUG_LOG a path outside the public folder, and turn it off as soon as you can (the constants back to false, then the file deleted).
More: https://developer.wordpress.org/advanced-administration/debug/debug-wordpress/
